    {
      "id": "claim_270348d6b84f4852bd110ae49e627305",
      "statement": "The `docker-outside-of-docker` feature fronts the VM socket with a socat relay whose half-close timeout defaults to 0.5 s. `docker exec` half-closes stdin immediately, so socat tears the relay down mid-response — fast commands return exit 0 with no output, and the seam looks healthy under any quick probe while real work fails. The fix is to set `DOCKER_HOST=unix:///var/run/docker-host.sock`, already applied in `.devcontainer/sandbox/devcontainer.json`; contexts that do not inherit `containerEnv` must pass it explicitly. `verify-engine-seam.sh` guards it with a deliberately slow (2 s) probe, since a fast one would assert nothing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.devcontainer/sandbox/devcontainer.json#L225-L253",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7d787c6f1b2f362bea42664ecc300d9499c3f4f5c1212278e987f8ac3fa11218:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L355-L386",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:250caa66d4c6b3b1ab43c6e2da5d61d59727350d514acb217b4fc26e9f44c8ef:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1336a6cd9d764aa0a75fca600b5b7d46",
      "statement": "In the sandbox, the in-VM firewall (`ipset`/`iptables`) is not used; enforcement is the host-side policy outside the VM, and triage order is therefore host policy first, in-VM second — the opposite of the Docker Desktop path. The in-VM layer is not merely unused but hazardous there: under `--network=host` the container shares the VM's network namespace identically, so a default-DROP would be VM-wide. `nc -z <ip> 443` reports OPEN against a blocked destination because the proxy accepts TCP and refuses at TLS; from the dev container a refusal is `rc=6` (NXDOMAIN) with `curl` writing `000`, so the exit code, not the status code, is the signal.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.devcontainer/assert-egress-governed.sh#L1-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6003a35579732554831b7a63a59a389dd917fc85cb0cd0cf7444efedfe04694e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L185-L262",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a8c0866e0e291385e913748cf2279267a873f4e938131215bac616e0ab740f92:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a7c0a0fc6da6473c82edbb1d1d65d7e7",
      "statement": "Git must run inside the dev container, not in the VM shell. The VM user and container user previously had different UIDs (uid 1000 vs a different uid), causing git writes from the VM shell to be unwritable by the container user. Fixed 2026-08-17: `toolchain.Dockerfile` now creates `coder` at 1000:1000.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L1-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:276c5cdeab693441ce0ff737154f9892d269fbd1cf0af75a8efd1dd1b85df16e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_58ba995640414751b0850e3a4e0a7274",
      "statement": "Every `containerEnv` entry in a devcontainer.json becomes an `ENV` instruction in the generated derived image, making it permanently readable in `Config.Env` and history layers. Measured on the derived image on 2026-09-19: all four credential values were present in `Config.Env` and in three history layers. Credentials must go through the runtime env file written by `.devcontainer/gen-container-secrets-env.sh`, not declared in `containerEnv`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L141-L141",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b3679ee6b341a7fcbf81c7e6cd5b32a4eeca4af2aafed9163193d6fbbac62c18:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L127-L175",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fbbdef1ca33aecc582a2af7d209114e50bfda178045a406671b8af13e30dddc8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7872ae1c6b2f448bb6b8e4f20104b3bf",
      "statement": "`sbx` is pinned at v0.47.0 (upgraded from v0.43.0 on 2026-10-08). Because it enforces this environment's isolation and egress, an upgrade is a security-relevant change with a required ritual: read the intervening release notes for network-policy, `--network=host`, port-publishing, idle-stop, secret-injection and template changes; capture the before-state with `verify-reboot-survival.sh --capture`; re-run the harness plus the host-side `verify-sandbox-egress.sh --audit-check`; re-run the G5 sibling-egress refusal explicitly; and record the new version in the runbook. Several behaviours here are version-specific and undocumented.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L1354-L1461",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3acc887577a9c715f37e67da16ab559fb20dfb3e061469509f80f6f683f615e6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0066081d711c4a96974a3e24aac1ba3f",
      "statement": "`sbx run` can report `docker daemon failed to start inside the sandbox` while dockerd is healthy: restoring this VM's 20 `restart: unless-stopped` containers takes 54–101 s and overruns sbx's compiled-in dockerd-readiness budget, so sbx aborts, the CLI exits, and the ~30 s idle-stop kills a working VM. There is no knob (no flag, `DOCKER_SANDBOXES_*`/`SBX_*` variable, settings file, or daemon option; v0.43.0 did not raise it). `scripts/open-sandbox.ps1` works around it by treating the exit code as a claim and SSH answering as evidence, waiting up to a 120 s deadline; a bare `sbx run` still shows the false failure.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L834-L944",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f4006fdb3353e1a539d5b7404ff18dac5604d7a4250c30ae99c396dbf9b83501:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/open-sandbox.ps1#L126-L164",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ac15d5eeeec9e2a958d0789ed4bc214b0fa964bb55bb6358146aefdf32f59655:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cb7a2d7215834dcdb76cffb42df94b08",
      "statement": "The sandbox microVM idle-stops roughly 30 seconds after the last session disconnects — hardcoded, with no configuration knob. A \"missing\" environment usually just idle-stopped and nothing is lost, but long unattended jobs die unless a session is held (`ssh mcm.sbx 'sleep 5400'` in another window, work launched with `setsid nohup … &`); the dev container returns by itself via `--restart=always`, while the agent stack deliberately does not.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L110-L119",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8819a54f3cfe3e7bb98a813c20f0cdb5ce090f245a42b952cefec5c6678a60db:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L440-L464",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:054a621f6b7ea091bdef8cd32ad0612bceaa51f6de759b206ce0d9f2fc75a623:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8bec03500ec240ed993844be694b375d",
      "statement": "In `sbx` v0.47.0 the VM-shell egress refusal body changed to HTTP 403 `Approval required for <host>:<port>.` (from `Blocked by network policy`). A harness check keyed to the old marker reported a deny-by-default breach that had not occurred, so both verify scripts now accept both bodies. The new body also queues a pending approval (`sbx policy approval ls`), and `sbx policy approval respond … allow` is a second path that widens egress while bypassing the canonical `.devcontainer/egress-allowlist.json` — it must never be used; add the destination to the canonical file and apply the generated rule instead, and use `dismiss` to clear the queue.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L1361-L1372",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b8f0472e4a930012856abada3e4622f27d8020f3aa073fa352a2aca0ab2d6fc8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L213-L240",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b24c73b32e985b11dfa38c699329c2778ab72e58a2915838459f4d326c3e7c47:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0360611fc9834c2496ff05414bfae932",
      "statement": "Because several concurrent Claude sessions can share `/workspaces/mcm` and its git index and checked-out branch (five were measured on 2026-09-18), any branch work must happen in a git worktree under `/home/coder/worktrees/<slug>`, never `/workspaces/.worktrees/…` (`/workspaces` is not writable). The `node_modules` symlink into the main checkout suffices for `node --test` and the `scripts/*.mjs` gates but not for any `pnpm nx` target, which fails with `ERR_PNPM_UNSAFE_MODULES_DIR` and needs a real `CI=true pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` inside the worktree; a worktree does not survive a container rebuild, so branches must be pushed before risky container operations.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CLAUDE.md#L7-L7",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:657251edf9b7a1ba2b50aede4fd41dcf7b6072f71687c7f518cf44050be56c94:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer.md#L303-L399",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dd523e7d1c12121022b8cee52e791a6dd28a0daac9b4d23b46e8de5053549a30:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_62d970d06ad14832a07ded286677d0fb",
      "statement": "The sandbox dev container's credentials are passed with `docker run --env-file` wired through `runArgs`, with the file written by `.devcontainer/gen-container-secrets-env.sh` as `initializeCommand` — which the devcontainer CLI runs on the VM before create, because `--env-file` fails on a missing file. `docker exec` still inherits the values and the image does not, but they remain visible in `docker inspect <container>`; `remoteEnv` is not usable here because it does not reach `ssh mcm.sbx` + `docker exec`. `devcontainer up` does not recreate the container when only `runArgs`/`containerEnv` change — it reattaches and reports success while the old image keeps running — so `--remove-existing-container` is required and verification must inspect the container rather than the command's exit code.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.devcontainer/gen-container-secrets-env.sh#L1-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:baa9dcb2e21f4b20a5c17e2ec032b8c8e1f1e19831c237c891729983f5d9496b:"
        },
